  "security_implications": "The SHA-2 instance processes data to produce a digest (sha2_digest). The wipe interface is disabled (wipe_secret_i=0, wipe_v_i=0), so any secret internal state cannot be cleared after use, potentially leaving sensitive data in the engine. Critical status outputs (digest_on_blk_o, hash_running_o, idle_o) are unconnected, preventing software from monitoring engine state and potentially causing incorrect sequencing or race conditions. The sha2_mode input is not validated locally, risking misconfiguration that could lead to weakened hashing or security bypass.",
